# Menu click routing
#
# Covers what screenshots cannot: that a click lands on the right widget.
# Exercises the real system pipeline (ResolveHitTarget -> HandleClicks), not
# a test harness driving the systems by hand.
#
# The menu bar is the case afterhours D3 was about -- a trigger sits inside a
# holder div, and menu items sit inside a list, so every one of these clicks
# has to reach a nested control rather than its container.

goto_screen menu_showcase
resize 1280 720
wait 0.3

# Bottom defaults open, so its items are on screen and Edit's are not.
expect_text "Save"
expect_no_text "Undo"

# Clicking a trigger must reach the trigger, not the holder div wrapping it.
click_ui menu_Edit_trigger
wait 0.3
expect_text "Undo"

# ...and opening Edit takes focus, which dismisses Bottom.
expect_no_text "Save"

# Clicking an item must reach the item, not the tray behind it. The tray
# carries its own HasClickListener, so this is the nested-control case D3 is
# about.
#
# Asserted on the status line, not on the menu disappearing: the menu closes on
# focus loss whatever the click hits, so "Undo is gone" is true even when the
# tray swallowed it. The status only changes when menu_list returns a chosen
# index, which needs the item's own listener to have fired.
expect_text "Edit menu open / placed below anchor"
click_ui menu_Edit_menu_item_3
wait 0.3
expect_text "Edit item chosen"

screenshot menu_click_routing
